cxi_user_force_avoid_wc.patch
=============================

Test patch. Adds a writable module parameter to cxi_user that takes the
existing CONFIG_ARM64 avoid_writecombine branch of ucxi_mmap(), i.e. maps
CQ launch pages with pgprot_device instead of pgprot_writecombine. Only
cxi_user changes; cxi_ss1 is untouched, so only cxi_user needs to be
reloaded and HSN networking (cxi_eth) stays up.


Build (on the node, with the installed dkms source)
-----------------------------------------------------

  PATCH=$PWD/cxi_user_force_avoid_wc.patch     # run from this directory
  SRC=$(ls -d /usr/src/cray-cxi-driver-1.0.0-SHS*)
  for v in stock patched; do
      d=/usr/src/cray-cxi-driver-wc$v
      cp -a $SRC $d
      sed -i "s/^PACKAGE_VERSION=.*/PACKAGE_VERSION=\"wc$v\"/" $d/dkms.conf
      dkms add -m cray-cxi-driver -v wc$v
  done
  (cd /usr/src/cray-cxi-driver-wcpatched && patch -p1 < $PATCH)
  for v in stock patched; do
      dkms build -m cray-cxi-driver -v wc$v -k $(uname -r)
      zstd -d -f /var/lib/dkms/cray-cxi-driver/wc$v/$(uname -r)/aarch64/module/cxi-user.ko.zst \
           -o /tmp/cxi-user-$v.ko
  done

  # the stock rebuild must match the running module
  modinfo -F srcversion /tmp/cxi-user-stock.ko; cat /sys/module/cxi_user/srcversion

dkms build only builds; nothing is installed.


Swap cxi_user (node idle, no /dev/cxi* users)
-----------------------------------------------

  devs=$(ls /sys/class/cxi)
  for d in $devs; do systemctl stop cxi_rh@$d; done
  rmmod cxi_user
  insmod /tmp/cxi-user-patched.ko
  for d in $devs; do systemctl start cxi_rh@$d; done

Restore the stock module the same way, with "modprobe cxi-user" instead of
insmod, or reboot.


Test
----

  cd ../reproducer
  FORCE_AVOID_WC=0 PHASES="spec" ./run.sh
  FORCE_AVOID_WC=1 PHASES="spec spectgt read" ./run.sh
  FORCE_AVOID_WC=0 PHASES="spec" ./run.sh

With force_avoid_wc=1 the driver logs "Broken PCIe write-combine detected
on this platform ..." for every launch page mapping.


Result (GH200, SHS 13.1.0, kernel 6.4.0-150600.23.125-64kb, one module load)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  force_avoid_wc  probe                          pri_mb_xlat_pf_addr_error
  0               spec, TXQ (cxi2)               9
  1               spec, TXQ (cxi2)               0
  1               spec, whole 64K page (cxi1)    0
  1               spec, TGT queue (cxi0)         0
  1               read, 8-byte load (cxi3)       1, RTRGT dw_len 2 (8 bytes)
  0               spec, TXQ (cxi2), again        9

~100k mispredicted attempts per spec probe. With write-combine the same
8-byte load is reported with dw_len 16 (a 64-byte line fill).

The cost of the device mapping on the low-latency command path was not
measured. As a rough CPU-side figure, 200k NOOP submissions took 0.035 s
(write-combine) vs 0.052 s (device).
